# Status

Documentation on `main` describes `main` and is labeled **development** until
a versioned release channel exists. Never use a future plan to fill a gap in
shipped behavior.

## Labels used in this manual

| Label | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| current | Implemented and documented from code/tests |
| experimental | Implemented but explicitly unstable (`??` defaults, GitHub archives) |
| planned | Not shipped (`:deep`, `@log`, production signing, installers, live demo hostnames) |
| removed | Must not be taught (`@on`, trailing `json`, crates.io install) |

## Known limits (author-visible)

- Loopback-only `rocci.toml` HTTP host
- CSP allows `unsafe-eval` for Datastar
- macOS `.app` is ad-hoc signed; no notarization
- Windows/Linux installers not implemented
- Live example hostnames planned until a staging deploy serves them
- Playground WASM mode does not snapshot HTML

Changelog and a version selector wait until two public versions exist.

**Related:** [Compatibility](/docs/reference/compatibility/), [Grammar](/docs/reference/language/grammar/).
